 ("How do emotion and reasoning errors each lead decisions away from what utility theory predicts?", "Emotions such as anger, anxiety or sadness change choices, and reasoning biases such as belief bias reduce logical judgments, so neither follows a purely rational standard.", [2,6,15,18]),
